/-!
# A273539: Number of active (ON, black) cells at stage 2^n-1 of the two-dimensional cellular automaton defined by "Rule 779", based on the 5-celled von Neumann neighborhood.

Source: https://oeis.org/A273539
Credit: @ddanila

Proof outline:
1. Certify a binary automaton against a four-parent cellular update. Its 451
   recurrence relations are closed under all eight input digits; the finite
   checks use kernel reduction, with the closure split into blocks of 32 rows.
2. At times 2^n-1 only time-digit 1 occurs. Ten boundary states prove that
   the rotated pattern is exactly a square boundary.
3. A parity invariant proves that Rules 779, 795, 843 and 859 agree at every
   generation. Relate Rule 779's OFF cells to the rotated machine from time 1.
4. Transfer the square boundary to the diamond |x|+|y|=t. Count its 4t cells
   by rows and derive the closed form, recurrence and formal generating function.

The machine and certificates are finite witnesses, not assumptions. Their
recurrences and their connection to the source dynamics are proved below.
The time-zero seed is handled separately; it is not an OFF-cell indicator.
-/

